OL,3,GNEWSADown's syndrome project promotes
OL,4,Ablack visibility
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe founders of an advocacy initiative
OL,7,Ffor black children with Down's syndrome
OL,8,Fhave said they launched their project
OL,9,Ftwo years ago due to a "lack of
OL,10,Frepresentation".
OL,12,FDanise Bartlett-Grant, who is one of
OL,13,Ffour mothers who co-founded the Black
OL,14,FChild Down Syndrome Project, said they
OL,15,Fwanted to create a platform for parents
OL,16,Fand carers to find advice, help and
OL,17,F"have conversations outside of the
OL,18,Flarger disabled community groups".
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
